	"FriendlyName": "ArcCast - Trajectory & Landing Preview",
	"Description": "The throw arc you can actually ship. The engine predicts the path but can only draw it with DrawDebugLine, and ENABLE_DRAW_DEBUG is 0 in Shipping - so the preview disappears exactly when the game goes out. ArcCast draws on UCanvas through AHUD instead: no material, no mesh, no Niagara, no asset of any kind, and it survives a cooked Shipping build. It also goes further than the engine's own prediction: the simulation continues through bounces instead of stopping at the first hit, every landing gets a verdict (Valid, TooSteep, Blocked, OutOfRange, NoGround) that colours the arc, the splash ring is conformed to the geometry point by point so it follows stairs and slopes instead of floating as a flat disc, and occluded stretches are drawn dashed and faint instead of shining through the wall. The whole simulation is also callable on its own, with no drawing at all, when you just need to know where a throw would land. ArcCast does not throw anything: no projectile, no damage, no replication. It is the preview next to your throwing system, not the throwing system.",
	"Category": "Gameplay",
